WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.900
In Ukraine, President

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.402
Volodymyr Zelensky comparing

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.070
Vladimir Putin's Russia

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.672
to Hitler's Nazi Germany.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.306
He says he's

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.107
introducing a bill

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:07.540
to change

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.842
Ukraine's official Victory Day

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.143
holiday to May 8th

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.878
so that it does not coincide

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.213
with Russia's May 9th

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:13.780
Victory Day

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.382
celebration on Tuesday,

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.116
marking the defeat

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.184
of course of Germany in 1945.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.387
Rehearsals for Moscow's annual parade

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.422
currently underway as you can see here.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.991
CNN's Clare Sebastian live in London.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.026
Clare victory day

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:26.960
an opportunity for Russia

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.661
to show off its military might.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.196
Can we expect the same this year

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.031
and does it reflect,

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:31.831
I guess, the reality

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.967
on the ground in Ukraine?

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.101
Yeah, no it doesn't

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.669
it significantly glosses over,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.337
of course, Christine,

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.905
the reality on the ground in Ukraine.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.407
On the one hand, victory day

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.374
this year will be somewhat

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.675
scaled back in Russia.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.476
Several regions

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.344
have announced, particularly

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.112
the ones closest to Ukraine,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.780
that they are either

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.748
canceling or scaling back

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.617
parades things like fireworks display,

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.519
many of them citing security concerns.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.119
But on the one hand,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.722
we will be seeing Russia try to put out

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.391
its top military capabilities in all

00:00:58.391 --> 00:00:59.959
while we're seeing signify

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.162
losses of equipment on the ground,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.063
we know that sanctions

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.330
are hurting their ability

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.099
to produce more quick enough.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.534
And we found evidence

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.301
that this means

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:08.768
that Russia

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.303
is having to dip so far

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.439
back into its historical stockpiles

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.007
that it's bringing out 80 year

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.608
old tanks onto the battlefield.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.176
Take a look.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:18.211
What a

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.145
missile will do is

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.180
fly over the tank,

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.348
then down and in 90 degrees

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.917
straight into the top of the turret,

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.952
which is less well defended.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.487
This scenario has played out

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.422
hundreds of times over the past

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.690
14 months.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.191
Ukraine

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.459
using Western weapons

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.495
to devastating effect.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.963
Russia, according to one recent

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.064
estimate, has lost up

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.532
to half its operational

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.335
tank fleet in this war.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.070
Now, Western officials say

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.338
Russia's dusting off

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.540
much older models to replace them.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.842
This gun was used on the issue.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.344
100 tank destroyer in 1944.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.812
So it's a Second World War

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.881
including the T-55

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.883
first built in the 1940s.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.684
This one now

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.152
housed at the Imperial War

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.421
Museum outside Cambridge.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.556
Satellite imagery for a storage facility

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.090
in Russia's

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.891
Far East

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.260
showing dozens of tanks have been removed

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.895
in the last year.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.963
This image showing the

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.465
T-55 at that same facility

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.835
video that first surfaced in March

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.171
also showing a trainload on the move

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.607
reportedly somewhere in Russia.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:20.940
The Russian

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.741
Ministry of Defense

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.144
hasn't confirmed their deployment,

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.845
but in recent weeks well connected

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.747
Russian bloggers have begun showing

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.249
T-55 caves in Russian

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.651
occupied territory in Ukraine.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.752
The so many of these are

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.787
manufactured over 100,000 altogether.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.688
And the parts,

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:36.656
the basic

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.825
mechanical parts are all interchangeable

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.261
So there will be vast stockpiles

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:41.661
of these.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:42.328
These appear

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:42.929
to be

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.030
the T-55

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.932
with a central piece of the Soviet

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:46.966
Union's Cold War

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:47.867
arsenal

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.601
helping crush

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.737
democratic uprisings in Eastern Europe

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.173
Hungary in 1956

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.175
the Prague Spring 12 years later.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.076
But by the time Iraq

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.211
used them in the Gulf War

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.713
in the early nineties we took out,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.116
all told, 14 T-55 tanks.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.451
They were already outclassed by us.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.620
M-1 Abrams and British challenges

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:09.956
Earlier versions of the

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.357
tanks NATO countries

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.159
are now supplying to Ukraine.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.129
I think face with Western weapons.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.098
Well the Russians must expect

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.733
very heavy casualties

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.002
if they expect to move forward

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.471
using that type of system.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.474
Experts say,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.510
behind the official propaganda.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.612
Russia cannot build new weapons

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.813
quick enough,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.381
but Western sanctions primarily

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:36.849
targeting Russia's access

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.351
to higher tech parts

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:38.851
for weapons,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.053
have made it much harder

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.387
for them to manufacture

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.822
more modern equipment,

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.891
older, simpler tanks like this.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.092
Thousands of them

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.827
just sitting in storage

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.629
provide an alternative.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.930
But this against, say,

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.532
a leopard two or a challenger.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.399
What happens

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.134
if it's a one on one tank engagement

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.236
over a reasonable distance?

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.337
This will lose every time.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.571
Putting in

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.072
would need

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.640
to close the built environment.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.041
This is adequate.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.677
It's also simpler to maintain and train

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.045
on the newer systems

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.380
and advantage for Russia's

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.581
mobilized troops.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.882
Dig a pit seated.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:10.783
Sit the tank in the pit

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.518
so you can only see the turret

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.720
and then that can be used

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.988
to defend the front line against

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:15.655
the counterattack.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:20.293
Russia is now digging in with everything

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.227
it has

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:21.961
as Ukraine

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:22.562
gets ready

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.931
for what may be its biggest

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.666
offensive yet.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.002
So, look, it's clear that

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.503
Ukraine in many ways

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.238
has the quality edge here

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.306
with the Western weapons,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.440
the NATO's standard weapons

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.075
that it's being supplied in particular

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:36.843
Those tanks,

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.510
Russia, though,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.044
may be able

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.346
to bring the quantity to bear,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.881
and that could be significant

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.915
on the battlefield, particularly

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.751
as it goes into defensive mode.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.252
If Ukraine launches

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.854
this counter offensive.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.122
But I think what this really shows,

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.990
Christine, is Russia's commitment

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.192
to keep this going, to bring everything

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.827
it can possibly get its hands on

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.963
to keep this attrition style war,

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.432
keep it going essentially. Remarkable.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:04:59.732
All right,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.867
Clare Sebastian, thanks for that.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:03.536
Look at Russian attacks today

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.371
hitting across Ukraine.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.572
Let's get you to our international

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.074
diplomatic editor, Nic Robertson,

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.176
who is in eastern Ukraine.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.678
Forgive my voice. And Nic,

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.280
there are rumors that

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.815
Ukraine is set to launch

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.217
its long anticipated counter offensive.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.420
We just heard Nick Paton Walsh

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.488
suggesting there is evidence

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.024
that we are about to see that.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.192
What is that evidence?

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:26.726
Nick, tell us

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:29.462
what's going on on the ground

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:31.764
Well,

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:32.932
there are restrictions

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.200
that reporters like us

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.768
have put on the air in Ukraine

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.071
that do not permit us to

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.173
to talk about troop movements.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.874
We see all locations

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.309
or numbers of troops.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:44.177
We've been around

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.178
the Eastern Front today,

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.179
and you can certainly hear

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.880
a lot of artillery fire

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.115
along the eastern front.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.284
But we've also been

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.720
we've also been sorry, that's the air

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.121
raid alarm

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.489
just being cleared around here,

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.825
which goes on and off quite a lot.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.393
But I think generally speaking,

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:03.529
when we speak to Ukrainian commanders,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.066
the perception that they want to give us

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.434
is that the counter

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.371
offensive is not about to happen

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.406
just yet. It will.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.475
But they say part of the psychology

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:16.909
of the counter offensive

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.044
and having the Russians

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.479
believe that it's coming

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:20.413
and that it's been imminent

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:22.081
for some time is drawing

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.083
a large number of Russian troops

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.651
into Ukraine.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.053
The Ukrainians say

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.454
while the Russians are at the front

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.322
lines, it's

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.524
hard to harder for the Russian forces

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.658
to get them

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:35.161
everything that they need, the resupply,

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:37.296
the food, the ammunition,

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.965
all of that, that it takes to sustain

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:40.299
an army in high readiness.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.434
And it also creates

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:42.201
poor morale,

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:43.269
they say, among the Russians

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:43.870
who are fearing

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.505
where is the counter-offensive

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.539
going to come?

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.874
There are no indications

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:48.408
being given

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:50.743
by Ukrainian officials

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.245
about where it might come

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:53.780
or when it might come.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.882
I think the hints

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.584
that we see on the ground here

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.220
are that the preparations are there,

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:05.091
but the information that's being provided

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:06.025
suggests

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:08.327
that it may not just be just yet.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:09.128
But, of course,

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:11.497
this is psychological warfare.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.801
So it's hard to discern that the

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.670
the accurate, most accurate narrative

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.039
And whenever

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.240
that counteroffensive

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.242
is, Zelensky is said,

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:24.710
and I quote him here,

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.614
evil has returned and will be defeated

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:31.384
whenever this counteroffensive starts.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.752
This is crucial.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:35.421
Many say this is sort of this

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:38.591
will be the big battle

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:41.861
Is that what it feels like on the ground?

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.263
It does.

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:46.532
We're here and we're out in the field.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:49.368
And we do get to talk to a lot of

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.804
senior Ukrainian military officials

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.072
And these conversations

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.774
are often off the record

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.342
or on our own background.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.678
But but what everyone will agree on

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:01.547
is that Russia has a huge military force

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:02.482
in the country.

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.617
Last estimate from the

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:06.219
defense intelligence here

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:09.922
was 369,000 troops, Russian troops

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.123
inside Ukraine.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:11.657
That's triple

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.593
the number at the time of the invasion.

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.495
The defenses are very heavily

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:16.596
well dug in.

00:08:16.596 --> 00:08:18.698
This will be, for the Ukrainians,

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:20.166
a tough offensive,

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:20.933
but it's one

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.201
that they must win

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:23.703
and it's one that they must use

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:25.271
the psychological warfare,

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:26.472
the strategy of trying

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:27.607
to deceive

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:28.908
the enemy in one area

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:31.377
and attack them in another

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:31.844
But

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:33.679
but the vital fact

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.515
that they all understand

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:36.883
and know to be true

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:39.252
is that they must break through.

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:40.753
They must show that they can get

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:42.555
a strong and fast advance

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:43.823
to put pressure on Russia

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.091
and create chaos

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:46.225
in the Russian ranks

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.560
and show

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.661
their political

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:51.197
and military allies in the West

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.832
that the investment

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:54.333
of money and equipment

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.469
and support has been worthwhile.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:09:00.573
They're aware that Western backing for

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.475
for Ukraine

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:03.910
is potentially at stake

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.778
or the level of backing.

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:07.813
If they can't convince that they can

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.216
they can take territory back this year.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:10.950
They're worried

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:11.851
that a stalemate

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:12.552
could develop

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:15.021
and political sustainability

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:16.088
among their allies

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.057
may be maybe harder to maintain

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:19.058
this level of support.

